Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Handle-slide & Homotopy Calculator", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.892826618303*^9, 3.8928266698514757`*^9}, 
   3.892826881127287*^9},
 CellTags->
  "Introduction",ExpressionUUID->"db819519-ad2b-4af5-8654-61c2dde4a397"],

Cell["\<\
This code is designed to be able to draw representatives of morphisms in the \
band category in a \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]square with bands\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] model with all the bands isolated on the right hand \
edge. It is also designed to perform the two necessary topological moves on \
said pictures being 
(a) handle-slides: this is where we slide one band over another band and \
track what happens to embedded curves,
(b) homotopy: this is where we can smoothly deform the embedded curves on the \
surface. We note that the notion of homotopy employed here is as simple as \
possible - i.e. we want to remove redundant interactions of curves with bands \
by \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]pulling strings tight\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], e.g. \
the picture:\
\>", "Text",
