Cell["\<\
With the Htpe and Hslide operations defined now, it is not too difficult to \
imagine writing a function which tries to find an optimal representative for \
a given picture so I think this should definitely be a future extension.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8928314253543825`*^9, 3.892831521635186*^9}, {
  3.894081533744683*^9, 
  3.8940815413563423`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6989eb97-ddbd-42e6-bdfe-\
b6b96b8d1bec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["NOTE:",
  FontVariations->{"Underline"->True}],
 " So far I haven\[CloseCurlyQuote]t really added a mechanism for removing \
closed curves (especially ones with non-trivial homotopy classes). The Htpe \
function will remove contractible closed curves in the simple situation below:"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8928312788880415`*^9, 3.8928314174955926`*^9}, {
  3.892831525950076*^9, 
  3.892831575017742*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dc448d59-c64b-45b5-b119-\
46e72ddad555"],

